    <div><span class="eg-eyebrow">A readable application record</span><h2>Give debugging a useful starting point.</h2><p class="eg-lede">Which node was active? What facts had it accepted? What history did it see? What warning accompanied the turn?</p><p>The session document gives these questions a common home, alongside model usage and decision diagnostics. Inspect the record with your own tools or provide a carefully selected excerpt to an AI debugging assistant.</p><ul class="eg-check-list"><li>Typed node facts and graph-wide context</li><li>Named histories and the active stage</li><li>Usage, warnings, errors, and decisions</li><li>Schema versions and migration hooks</li></ul><a class="eg-link" href="/ezgraph/docs/developer-guide/state-context-and-history/">Explore state, history, and persistence <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><p class="eg-note" style="margin-top:20px">Application session snapshots have a different recovery boundary from LangGraph checkpoints. <a href="/ezgraph/compare/langgraph/#state-and-sessions">See the distinction.</a></p></div>
